Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?style(play):=20apply=20"Direction=20A"=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20calm,=20clear,=20high-contrast=20child=20surface?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Restyle the child-facing play surface for children with low vision:
flat cream ground (no gradient/blobs), navy ink, thick outlines and solid
shadows, larger instruction / speaker / confirm button, and a selection
state that never relies on colour alone (thicker outline + yellow halo +
✓ badge). The dark theme becomes the high-contrast variant (navy ground,
white tiles, yellow actions).

Visual only: no game logic, props, copy or instruction placement changed
(the child instruction stays in the top-right corner).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013sR5aMGdnxhQYKYTJi69z3
